# Third-Party Licenses

Inventory of third-party code distributed with this repository: Go modules linked into the binary
and npm packages bundled into the embedded web console (`web/dist`, embedded by `web/embed.go`).

Generated: 2026-10-22. Scope: Go module `github.com/LeXwDeX/Code-Review-For-Gitlab-CE`.

## How this inventory was built

- Go: `go list -m -json all` reported 129 modules (1 main module, 128 third-party). The host/test
  build set was resolved with `go list -deps -test ./...`: 42 third-party modules provide packages
  imported by the main module, and these 42 are exactly the `require` entries in `go.mod`. All 42
  were read from `GOMODCACHE` (`go env GOMODCACHE`).
- 23 further modules exist in the module graph and had a local module cache copy; their license files
  were also read. They are not compiled into this build and are listed separately.
- 63 modules exist only in the module graph, with no local copy. They are not compiled into this build;
  their license files could not be read offline (see "Modules without a discoverable license file").
- npm: `web/package-lock.json` (lockfileVersion 3) marks 9 packages as production dependencies (no
  `dev`/`devOptional` flag). Each `web/node_modules/<pkg>/LICENSE*` file was read.

