## Verification method / limitations

This is a factual inventory, not legal advice and not a legal clearance.

- Go versions come from `go list -m -json all`; npm versions from `web/package-lock.json`.
- License names were identified by reading license file text, not taken from module metadata.
- Only top-level license files (`LICENSE`, `LICENSE.md`, `LICENSE.txt`, `COPYING`, `NOTICE` and
  close variants) were opened, plus the `modernc.org` bundled notices listed above. Copyright
  headers inside individual source files were not audited.
- Indirect modules are included. The build set was computed with `go list -deps -test ./...`, which
  covers test imports of packages in this repository; no third-party module appeared beyond the 42.
- File-level attribution requirements (for example Apache-2.0 NOTICE files and BSD clauses) are
  recorded only as the license and copyright line. Redistribution still requires keeping the
  license texts and notices that the licenses require.
- The 63 graph-only modules without a local copy could not be read; their licenses are unknown here.
- npm production lock entries carry resolved URLs and integrity hashes; `npm ci` installed the
  locked tree during this verification. License files were read from `web/node_modules`.
- The checked-in release bundle `licenses/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` is generated by
  `scripts/licensebundle` and checked by CI. It covers `GOROOT/LICENSE`, the Linux/amd64 server
  module set, and npm production packages.

